# Semgrep ignore list.
#
# NOTE: the presence of this file REPLACES semgrep's built-in defaults, which
# skip *_test.go. That default is exactly the gap this file closes: the two
# credentials this repo's SAST gate was added to catch
# (internal/redact/redact_test.go:46,97) live in a _test.go file, and without
# an explicit override here they are silently skipped rather than scanned.
# The usual excludes (vendor, node_modules, VCS dirs) are restated below
# rather than inherited, since the built-in list no longer applies once this
# file exists.

# --- Go tests ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT excluded. Test fixtures are fabricated credentials by
# nature, which the credential rule (.semgrep/hardcoded-credentials.yml)
# flags — that is the finding this gate exists to surface, not noise to
# silence. Annotate a genuine fixture in place with
# `// nosemgrep: hardcoded-credential-literal` instead of excluding its file.

# --- Dependencies and build output ------------------------------------------
vendor/
node_modules/
build/
dist/

# --- Virtualenvs -------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
.env/

# --- VCS and tooling ---------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.svn/
.hg/
# Rule fixtures whose whole purpose is to contain deliberate violations;
# GOSEC_FLAGS / SEMGREP_FLAGS in the Makefile also exclude this directory
# explicitly, this is belt-and-suspenders for any scan invoked without them.
.semgrep/
